<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>BackDoor</title>

    <link rel = "stylesheet" href="generalStyle.css">
    <link rel = "stylesheet" href="contactUsStyle.css">
    <script src="contactUsScript.js" defer></script>

    <link rel="stylesheet"href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"/>

</head>

<%- include('partials/navbar') %>

<body>
    
    <main class = "contact-main">

        <h1 style = "font-size: 48px; margin-bottom: 1vh;">Contact Us</h1>

        <div class = "contact-container">

            <div class = "contact-container-child">
                
                <form id = "gmail-form" action="/contact/send" method="POST">

                    <p class = "subject-text">Full Name</p>
                    <input class = "subject-style" name = "subject-header" id = "subject-header" type="text" placeholder="Enter your full name here..." required>
                    
                    <br>

                    <p class = "subject-text">Email Address</p>
                    <input class = "subject-style" name = "subject-email" id = "subject-email" type="text" placeholder="Enter your email address here..." required>
                    
                    <br>

                    <p class = "subject-text">Subject Body</p>
                    <textarea class = "subject-style" name = "subject-body" id = "subject-body" type="text" placeholder="Enter your message here..." required></textarea>
                    
                    <br>

                    <section style = "display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; width: 80%">
                        <button name = "subject-submit" id = "subject-submit">Submit</button>
                        <p id = "subject-submit-text" style = "font-weight: bold; text-align: right; font-size: 18px; opacity: 0;">Placeholder</p>
                    </section>

                </form>

            </div>

            <div class = "contact-container-child">
                <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>

                <section class="faq-section">
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>What is BackDoor?</summary>
                        <p>
                            BackDoor is a save-file editor and research tool for supported games.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Do I need to back up my save file?</summary>
                        <p>
                            Yes. Always make a copy before replacing or editing any save file.
                            The reccomended approach is:
                        </p>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Create a folder in your downloads folder</li>
                            <li>Name it "Save File Copies" or something</li>
                            <li>Copy all of your original save files into this folder</li>
                            <li>Then use the files from THIS folder for BackDoor</li>   
                            <li>When editing is finished, download, replace the copied file, then replace the original</li>
                            <li><em>Make sure a backup exists somewhere</em></li>      
                        </ol>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Why are only some games supported?</summary>
                        <p>
                            Every game stores save data differently, 
                            so each game needs its own decoder and encoder.
                            For example, Hyperlight Drifter encodes their saves in base64,
                            while Undertale doesn't encode their files at all.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Also, every game has a different structure. Hyperlight's is
                            all in one line, while Celeste's is in XML.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Can BackDoor edit every save file?</summary>
                        <p>
                            No. Some saves are encrypted, compressed, binary, or undocumented.
                            For example, we tried to implement <em>Subnautica</em> but their saves are in binary.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Unless there is <em>Subnautica</em> save documentation online, there is no way
                            to reliably decode these files.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Can I suggest a game?</summary>
                        <p>
                            Yes. Users can contact us with game suggestions, 
                            especially if they know the save format or location.
                        </p>
                    </details>
                </section>
            </div>

        </div>

    </main>

</body>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>

</html>